# Research Insight: COVID-19 Vaccine Efficacy – A Clinical-Grade Synthesis
*Synthesized by Maverick AI Suite (GPT-OSS 120B)*

**Synthesis**
Since the emergence of SARS-CoV-2, >10 vaccine platforms have received regulatory authorization. Below is a concise, evidence-based overview of the efficacy (clinical trial VE) and real-world effectiveness of the most widely used products, with emphasis on the impact of viral variants, waning immunity, and booster strategies.

---

### 1. mRNA Platforms (Highest Potency)
**Pfizer-BioNTech (BNT162b2)**
*   **Efficacy:** 95% (95% CI 90.3-97.6) against wild-type.
*   **Real-World (Delta):** 91% vs infection, 94% vs hospitalization.
*   **Omicron:** 88% initially; restores to >90% against severe disease with 3rd dose (BA.5).
*   **Safety:** Myocarditis risk ≈12-40/million (young males); highly favorable risk-benefit.

**Moderna (mRNA-1273)**
*   **Efficacy:** 94.1% (95% CI 89.3-96.8) against wild-type.
*   **Note:** Higher antigen dose (100 µg) yields 1.5-2x higher neutralising titres than Pfizer.
*   **Real-World (Delta):** 86% vs infection, 93% vs hospitalization.
*   **Durability:** 4-dose series maintains >90% protection against severe disease up to 6 months.

---

### 2. Adenoviral Vector Platforms
**AstraZeneca (ChAdOx1-nCoV-19)**
*   **Efficacy:** 70.4% overall (90% against severe disease).
*   **Real-World (Delta):** 80-85% effectiveness against hospitalization; 60-70% against infection.
*   **Waning:** More pronounced than mRNA; heterologous mRNA booster is now standard of care.
*   **Safety:** TTS risk ≈4-6 cases/million.

**Janssen (Ad26.COV2.S - Single Dose)**
*   **Efficacy:** 66.9% against moderate-to-severe disease; 85% against hospitalization.
*   **Real-World (Delta):** 71% vs infection, 93% vs hospitalization.
*   **Omicron Support:** Single-dose schedule simplified logistics; mRNA booster restores high protection.

---

### 3. Recombinant Protein Platforms
**Novavax (NVX-CoV2373)**
*   **Efficacy:** 89.7% symptomatic; 100% against severe disease in trials.
*   **Real-World (Delta):** 86-90% vs infection; 96% vs hospitalization.
*   **Omicron:** ~50% (2 doses) → ~80% (mRNA booster). Slower waning observed compared to viral vectors.

---

### 4. Inactivated Platforms
**Sinovac (CoronaVac) / Sinopharm (BBIBP-CorV)**
*   **Efficacy:** CoronaVac (50-60%), BBIBP-CorV (78%).
*   **Real-World:** 65-70% vs severe disease (Delta); <30% vs Omicron infection.
*   **Note:** Rapid waning; 2-dose series insufficient beyond 4-5 months without boosters.

---

**Analysis**
**Durability & Strategic Boosting**
VE typically declines by ~6-8% per month after the third month. **Heterologous boosting** (e.g., Adenoviral primary → mRNA boost) is highly effective, often yielding superior neutralising titres compared to homologous schedules.

\boxed{Recommendation: mRNA boosters are the primary mechanism for restoring >90% protection against severe outcomes in the Omicron era.}

---
*Sources: US CDC, UK NHS, Clinical Phase III Reports.*
